\q1 \v 1 \w Hallelujah|strong="H01984"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03050"\w*!\f + \fr 112:1 \ft Or \fqa Hallelu YAH\ft , meaning \fqa Praise the LORD\ft . This psalm is an acrostic poem, each line beginning with the successive letters of the Hebrew alphabet.\f*
\b 
\q1 \w Blessed|strong="H00835"\w* \w is the man|strong="H00376"\w* \w who fears|strong="H03373"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*,
\q2 \w who greatly|strong="H03966"\w* \w delights|strong="H02654"\w* \w in His commandments|strong="H04687"\w*.
